{{Quote|Okay, the valves in quadrant D are secure.|A First Order scuba trooper, to their fellow trooper|audio=QuadrantD-NoEscapePart1.flac|<ref name="No Escape Part 1" />}}
'''Quadrant D''' was a quadrant of the [[Trantor-class supertanker fuel depot|supertanker fuel depot]] ''[[Colossus]]''.<ref name="No Escape Part 1" /> In [[34 ABY]],<ref name="Date">{{ResistanceDate|1|20}}</ref> after the [[Mission to contact the Resistance|submerging]] of the ''Colossus'' by the [[Resistance]] [[spy]] [[Kazuda Xiono]] into the [[ocean]]s of<ref name="No Escape Part 1" /> the [[planet]] [[Castilon]],<ref name="Databank">{{Databank|first-order-scuba-troopers|First Order SCUBA troopers}}</ref> two [[First Order SCUBA trooper]]s carried out patrols of the [[Supertanker fuel depot|station]]. At one point during their patrols, [[Unidentified First Order SCUBA trooper 1|one]] of the [[trooper]]s reported to the [[Unidentified First Order SCUBA trooper 2|other]] that the valves located in quadrant D were secured.<ref name="No Escape Part 1" />

==Behind the scenes==
Quadrant D was first mentioned in "[[No Escape: Part 1]],"<ref name="No Escape Part 1" /> the twentieth episode of the [[Star Wars Resistance Season One|first season]] of the animated television series ''[[Star Wars Resistance]]'',<ref name="Insider">{{InsiderCite|190|Resistance Revisited|''Resistance'' Revisited}}</ref> which aired on [[March 10]], [[2019]].<ref name="Disney release">{{DisneyPress|wdtv=1|url=disneychannel/shows/star-wars-resistance/episodes|text=Star Wars Resistance}}</ref>

